commit 05c7bd71797d0455570b63d29cea64f283226fef
Author: Marco Machado <marco.machado@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 23 02:26:05 2026 -0300

    Bring the World Network to its UX spec: Sprint 11 stories IF-016 to IF-035
    
    src/ui/WorldMap.tsx: failed banner reads ROSTER EMPTY // NO CONTRACT CAN BE
    TAKEN; contract rows give the actual lock cause (CAMPAIGN LOST); the
    first-visit card is not aria-modal and using the clock dismisses it; Garrison
    STRAINED prints the notice tone; Unrest ink and bar follow calm / pressure /
    crisis; empty Feed prints -- CHANNEL OPEN --; the duplicate left INFLUENCE
    panel is gone and RESOURCE POOL is now INTEL (level, n / 100); each Influence
    action prints its effect as text under the button; the sector panel scrolls
    so OPEN CONTRACTS keeps its row.
    src/ui/worldOnboard.ts: clockUse seam (IF-019). src/ui/worldChrome.ts:
    unrestTone, lockReason, intelGate shared by rows and markers. src/ui/bits.tsx:
    SegBar notice tone.
    src/ui/ui.css: 10 px / 12 px type floors; Ink Dim text reads Ink inside .wm
    (token unchanged elsewhere); Ink Faint off text; nav labels in Ink; locked
    and disabled rows dim the frame, not the text; 24x24 hit areas; the card
    wrap no longer takes clicks (the transport was unusable under the card, a
    defect the probe found). Dead .red-dim / .wm-intel-val rules removed.
    design/ux/world-network.md: speed while paused resumes (as built, ruled);
    nav high-contrast row corrected (the earlier reading was a measurement error).
    production/epics/interface: 20 stories Complete with notes; EPIC table;
    production/sprint-status.yaml: 20 done. ROADMAP.md: gate plan.
    
    Verified: npm test x3 green before work (1627); final vitest 1642/1642,
    eslint clean, npm run build OK; probe ALL PASS 152 checks at 1280x720
    (production/qa/evidence/sprint-011/), watched failing on the as-built code
    and on two layout mutations; code review (ui-programmer, lead-programmer,
    qa-tester) APPROVED WITH SUGGESTIONS, applied.

